license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. For every k >= 0 an explicit rational nonnegative matrix C of order k+11, rank k+10 and nonnegative rank k+11 has a Kronecker square of nonnegative rank at most (k+10)^2+9, disproving the conjecture of Vandaele, Gillis, Glineur and Tuyttens that rank+(M x M) >= rank+(M) rank(M). Lean proofs and an exact rational certificate are included. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
